  "construction": {
    "basis": "reconstruction",
    "fidelity": "not-applicable",
    "note": "The finished design was read from Wichmann’s PG232 drawing and snapped to exact square-root-of-two values. Two radii and one unit-square diagonal set the half-side. The shared unit-star opening supplies the smaller star; the continued lines and exact parallels also close the larger star with 45-degree tips. The drawing gives no steps; we devised the construction.",
    "changes": "The compass steps, their order and the named points are ours. The finished tile edges follow the plain drawing. The palette is illustrative; no photograph was checked. The page gives no building attribution, so none is added.",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-26"
  },
